{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nParis is a spectacle of contradiction. Today we visited the abattoir, a grim reminder of the material basis of life, and then the Bourse, where the spirit of capital dances to a different tune. From Montmartre, one sees the whole city laid out like a logical proposition, every street a term in the argument of human freedom. I dined with Cousin and Fauriel. Fauriel, the editor of Greek folk songs, is a charming man; there is something in their ancient melodies that speaks to the soul, though I confess the political chatter of the Chamber of Deputies left me cold. It is all very lively, but I find myself missing the quiet order of our home and the sharp clarity of our conversations. The air here is thick with history, but I long for the peace of Berlin. Do not worry; I am well, if perhaps a bit tired.\n\nYours,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080527,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":198,"prompt_tokens":957,"total_tokens":1155,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-aNxOkpuYdx32e155h4zqHIHHvCjELkwE","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":957,"prompt_ms":897.976,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9383239289446186,"prompt_per_second":1065.7300417828537,"predicted_n":198,"predicted_ms":4675.188,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.731918781725888,"predicted_per_second":42.13734292610265}}